<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Muscovite War (1605–1618)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1605">1605</a>–<a href="/years/1618">1618</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Dymitriads</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Muscovite War of 1605–1618 was a series of conflicts in which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> intervened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/time-of-troubles">Time of Troubles</a>, first through the pretenders known as False Dmitry and from 1609 openly under Sigismund III. After the victory at Klushino (1610) Polish troops held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> until 1612, when a Russian national rising drove them out. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truce-of-deulino">Truce of Deulino</a> (1618) left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a> and other western lands to the Commonwealth.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-muscovite-war-1605-1618.jpg" alt="Polish–Muscovite War (1605–1618)" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rzeczpospolita_Dymitriads.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
